  "query_preview": "(Today through Monday)...\nIssued at 305 AM EDT Tue Sep 1 2026\n\nDry and hot weather conditions are expected through at least \nThursday as ridging and surface high pressure are impacting the \nregion. The surface high will place persistent southerly to \nsouthwesterly flow for central Indiana, allowing increasing hot and \nhumid conditions. Highs are expected to be in the 90s through at \nleast Thursday (possibly lingering into the start of the holiday \nweekend) with heat indices up to 105. Overnight lows will likely \nonly drop to the 70s, providing little relief. A heat advisory is in \neffect from this afternoon through most of the day Thursday. Drink \nplenty of fluids, limit time outdoors during peak heating, and check \nup on relatives and neighbors.\n\nModels show that the ridge will start to shift towards the end of \nthe week, but uncertainty ramps up from Friday and beyond as the \ndevelopment of the upper pattern becomes questionable in the \ndetails. Overall, the upper high looks to get pushed west as an \nomega block pattern sets up across the country. \n\nHowever, questions arise on the strength and locations of the upper \ntroughs/lows on either side of the high across the central part of \nthe country. This will have an impact on storm tracks and how much \ncooler air (cooler being a relative term) moves into the area.\n\nFor now, will allow a gradual cooldown from highs in the 90s on \nFriday to highs mainly in the 80s by Labor Day. Will have low PoPs \nat times at least through Sunday, but confidence is quite low on the \nspecifics of these.",
